hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19243","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: He was asked about a man greeting him while not in wudu. He said: Said narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from al-Hudayn Abi Sasan from al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh that he greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was performing wudu, and he did not return it to him until he performed wudu. He returned it to him and said: Nothing prevented me from returning to you except that I disliked to remember Allah except in purity. He said: Al-Hasan, because of this hadith, used to dislike to recite or remember Allah until he purified himself."
